  "source": "[\\unordered.pair:of{x, y}]\nDefines: Z is \\set\nusing: U is \\set\nwhen: x, y \"in\" U\nexpresses:\n. let: z is \\set\n  then:\n  . have: z \"in\"? Z\n    iff: (.z = x.) \\.or./ (.z = y.)\nDocumented:\n. called: \"unordered pair of $x?$ and $y?$\"\n. written: \"\\left \\{ x?, y? \\right \\}\"\n. description: \"The unordered pair $\\{x, y\\}$ is the set whose members are\n                precisely $x$ and $y$.\"\nId: \"17401045-fc72-4bd4-af7d-ab578690f81c\"",
